-- title:
--   Branch order at a node versus membership in (varpi,G)+Hⁿ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, and $a \in k$ with $a^{q^2}=a$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, write $A_K =$ `coeffSubring A K` for the intersection $A \cap K$ and `redRestrict red K` for the restriction of $red$ to it, and let $\varpi \in A_K$ be such that an element $c$ of $A_K$ reduces to $0$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi$. Let $g$ lie in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A_K (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of elements $f$ admitting two-variable polynomials $r,s$ over $A_K$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a,a^q)$ after reduction and $f \cdot \mathrm{ev}(s) = \mathrm{ev}(r)$, where $\mathrm{ev} =$ `modularEval (1 * q) A_K` evaluates $X_0 \mapsto j$, $X_1 \mapsto j_{1\cdot q}$ with coefficients mapped to constant series. Assume further that $g$, viewed as a Laurent series, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red` (the localisation of the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_{1\cdot q}$ at the kernel of coefficientwise reduction), that its image $\pi(g)$ under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in the subfield `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` of Laurent series over $k$ generated by $j$ and $j_1$, and that $\pi(g) \neq 0$. Then, for $n : \mathbb N$, one has $n \le \mathrm{ord}(\pi(g))$ at the place $(\mathrm{frobNodePair}\, q\, a).1 =$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, where $\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, if and only if $g$ belongs to the sum of the ideal of `modularLocalizedAtPoint` generated by $\mathrm{ev}(\varpi)$ and $\mathrm{ev}(X_1 - X_0^q)$ and the $n$-th power of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{ev}(X_0 - X_1^q)$.
--
--   This is the interface identifying the vanishing order along one branch at a supersingular node of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$ with an ideal-membership condition in the local ring at the node: modulo $(\varpi, j_q - j^q)$ the local ring becomes a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser the image of $H = j - j_q^{\,q}$, whose order at $\tilde\jmath = a$ is read off from `ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_jqModC_sub_pow_sq_eq_one`. It is used in the factorisation and unit-decomposition statements at the node (`exists_isPrime_mem_of_mul_eq_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair`, `exists_isUnit_and_eq_pow_mul_pow_mul_pow_mul_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_crossingPresentation`, `ne_zero_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_mem_ssJSet`); the hypothesis $\pi(g) \neq 0$ is needed because the order of $0$ is $0$ by convention.
-- source:
